  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;By virtue of the solid steel shutter design, this would create a hardened, obtrusive and out of character addition to the streetscene which projects a considerable distance from the established building line of High Road. This would cause harm to the overall character and appearance of the building and wider streetscene and is contrary to Policy 53 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The installation of solid, galvanised steel as a material for the shutters would create a hostile environment within the streetscene. This would harm the overall experience for users of the public footpath, particularly that of pedestrians and that of local residents, and would therefore impact negatively on the overall amenity of the area, contrary to Policy 57 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;By virtue of its siting the proposed development would create an obstruction within an area of publicly maintained highway footpath, thereby causing harm to pedestrian movements within High Road in an area of high footfall where the full width of the footpath is required. This is contrary to Policies 60 and 61 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024), which aim to provide a safe and welcoming environment for sustainable methods of travel.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
